Mail::DKIM2 - DKIM2 signing and verification for email

DESCRIPTION

Mail::DKIM2 implements the DKIM2 email authentication protocol as specified
in draft-clayton-dkim2-spec-08.  DKIM2 extends DKIM with chain-of-custody
tracking, allowing each hop in the delivery path to add a cryptographic
signature that covers all previous signatures and Message-Instance headers.

Features:

  - Sign outbound messages with DKIM2-Signature headers
  - Verify all signatures in the DKIM2 chain (not just the outermost)
  - Calculate, verify, and undo Message-Instance headers with diff recipes
  - Chain-of-custody validation via SMTP envelope domain matching
  - Streaming interface compatible with milter and other filter architectures

INSTALLATION

    perl Makefile.PL
    make
    make test
    make install

DEPENDENCIES

    Perl 5.20 or later
    Mail::DKIM 1.20200824 or later
    Email::MIME
    JSON
    Algorithm::Diff
    Digest::SHA
    MIME::Base64

For running the test suite:

    Path::Tiny
    Test keys and DNS data from https://github.com/dkim2wg/interop

SYNOPSIS

    # Sign a message
    use Mail::DKIM2::Signer;

    my $signer = Mail::DKIM2::Signer->new(
        Domain   => 'example.com',
        Selector => 'sel1',
        KeyFile  => '/path/to/private.pem',
    );
    $signer->PRINT($message_text);
    $signer->CLOSE;
    print $signer->as_string();

    # Verify a message
    use Mail::DKIM2::Verifier;

    my $verifier = Mail::DKIM2::Verifier->new();
    $verifier->set_pubkey_callback(\&find_key);
    $verifier->PRINT($message_text);
    $verifier->CLOSE;
    print $verifier->result_detail();

SEE ALSO

    https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-clayton-dkim2-spec/
    https://github.com/dkim2wg/interop

